### Practical 7: Authentication & Middleware Pipeline HTTP Tests
### Use with REST Client extension or import into Postman

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000

### 1. Health Check (Public Route)
GET {{baseUrl}}/health
Accept: application/json

### 2. User Registration - Validation Failure: Short Password (Rejected by Middleware)
POST {{baseUrl}}/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "student@charusat.edu.in",
  "password": "123"
}

### 3. User Registration - Validation Failure: Malformed Email (Rejected by Middleware)
POST {{baseUrl}}/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "not-an-email",
  "password": "ValidPassword123"
}

### 4. User Registration - Success (bcrypt hashed password)
POST {{baseUrl}}/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "student@charusat.edu.in",
  "password": "ValidPassword123",
  "name": "Charusat Student"
}

### 5. User Login - Failure (Wrong Password -> 401 Unauthorized)
POST {{baseUrl}}/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "student@charusat.edu.in",
  "password": "WrongPassword!"
}

### 6. User Login - Success (Generates JWT Token)
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "student@charusat.edu.in",
  "password": "ValidPassword123"
}

### Extract token for subsequent requests
@authToken = {{login.response.body.token}}

### 7. Access Protected Task Route WITHOUT Token (401 Unauthorized)
GET {{baseUrl}}/tasks
Accept: application/json

### 8. Access Protected Route WITH Tampered/Invalid Token (401 Unauthorized)
GET {{baseUrl}}/tasks
Authorization: Bearer invalid.jwt.token
Accept: application/json

### 9. Access Protected /me Endpoint (Supplementary Problem 1)
GET {{baseUrl}}/me
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Accept: application/json

### 10. Create Task - Validation Failure: Missing Title (Rejected by Middleware before DB)
POST {{baseUrl}}/tasks
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "description": "Missing title should be rejected by validation middleware"
}

### 11. Create Task - Validation Failure: Invalid Priority (Rejected by Middleware)
POST {{baseUrl}}/tasks
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Learn Middleware",
  "priority": "super-urgent"
}

### 12. Create Task - Success (Protected + Validated)
# @name createTask
POST {{baseUrl}}/tasks
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Complete Practical 7 JWT Pipeline",
  "description": "Implemented auth middleware, input validation, bcrypt password hashing",
  "priority": "high",
  "completed": false
}

@taskId = {{createTask.response.body.data._id}}

### 13. Get All Tasks (Protected)
GET {{baseUrl}}/tasks
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Accept: application/json

### 14. Get Task By ID (Protected)
GET {{baseUrl}}/tasks/{{taskId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Accept: application/json

### 15. Update Task (Protected + Validated)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/tasks/{{taskId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Complete Practical 7 JWT Pipeline (Verified)",
  "completed": true,
  "priority": "medium"
}

### 16. Delete Task (Protected)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/tasks/{{taskId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Accept: application/json
